APG PRODUCTION RELEASE CONTROL
Status: CURRENT

No APG release is complete merely because a commit exists on GitHub main or a Vercel deployment is READY.

Completion chain:
GitHub main
-> Vercel Production
-> https://australianproductguide.au public runtime
-> exact-SHA functional/browser/accessibility QA
-> APG Production Verification GREEN
-> APG Operating Backend reconciled to that exact release
-> RELEASE COMPLETE

GREEN means all critical Production controls pass, no known P0/P1 release blocker remains, GitHub Production Verification is successful, and current operating records have been reconciled.

AMBER means Production operates but a material non-critical defect, verification gap, or operating-record discrepancy remains.

RED means critical functionality, integrity, or verification failed, or the exact Production release cannot be established reliably.

Required release evidence:
- full and abbreviated Git SHA
- commit message/timestamp
- Vercel deployment ID/status/timestamp
- canonical Production URL/domain
- QA start/completion timestamps
- verification suite/version and result
- current catalogue/Amazon/runtime metrics when reconciled

If a fix creates a new SHA/deployment, relevant verification must be rerun against that new release. Evidence from different deployments must not be combined into one certification.

Detailed procedure: docs/PRODUCTION-RELEASE-CONTROL.md
Automated control: .github/workflows/production-smoke.yml
